==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|intefadah|intifadah|Intifada}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ar|اِنْتِفَاضَة||shaking off, uprising, insurrection}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Insurrection, a usually violent attempt to take control of a government.
# An [[uprising]], [[resistant]] struggle or [[rebellious]] protest, especially the [[Palestinian]] uprisings against [[Israel]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Thomas L. Friedman|title=Israelis, Palestinians and Their Neighbors Worry: Is This the Big One?|work=The New York Times|date=2021-05-11|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/05/11/opinion/jerusalem-rockets-israel.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=But unlike the '''Intifadas''' that began in 1987 and 2000, when Israel had someone to call to try to turn it off, there is no Palestinian on the other end of the phone this time {{...|— or, if there is, he’s a 15-year-old on his smartphone, swiping orders and inspiration from TikTok, the video app often used by young Palestinians to challenge and encourage one another to confront Israelis.}}}}

